      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6687833::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prolonged annealing at 600°C, 750°C, or 900°C can produce varying, generally higher degrees of local chemical order than rapid quenching.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6687833::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10041143::web::028::discussion_and_conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local chemical order produces a spatially rugged energy landscape and a range of local planar or shear-fault energies in NiCoCr.",
